Author: Niko1221 <Niko1221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 13 01:24:55 2026 +0200

    Commit graph: every GDN layer's conv history + state, and every QSA layer's tail restore + indexer append, in one launch each (STRATA_COMMIT_BATCH, default on; =0 keeps the per-layer loop)
    
    The per-layer commit was ~98 graph nodes; it runs between a window and the draft round, and on HIP the round
    waits for it (R9700 UD-Q4_K_XL: 2.35 -> 0.65 ms GPU). Each layer's arithmetic is the per-layer call's:
    gdn_parity (gdn_commit_layers vs the per-layer commit, n_keep 1-8) and qsa_parity (append_steps_layers vs
    copy + append_steps, 3 scalings) are bitwise. STRATA_COMMIT_TIMING=1 prints the commit graph's GPU time.

